  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper to goalkeeper, 6 v 4",
  "description": "Played on a 7v7 pitch split into thirds with cones. Six blue players and two goalkeepers must play the ball from one goalkeeper to the other and must have the ball in all three thirds on the way. Blue starts with two players in each third but may then move freely.\n\nFour red defenders start in the middle third. When a goalkeeper starts, two of them may go in and press in that third; the other two press when the ball heads the other way. All four may press in the middle. Blue scores a point when the ball reaches the goalkeeper without red touching it – then that goalkeeper starts the other way.\n\nIf red wins the ball they try to score in either goal, and blue must win it back at once. Make it harder with more red defenders. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn when you can – receive with your body open forwards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Create width and depth so there is always a pass past the nearest defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: play to the player who is free and facing the right way, not just the nearest one."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Red: press in pairs, close the forward pass and win the ball between the opponents' touches."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
